.Dd October 28, 2026
.Dt PLISTBUDDY 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm PlistBuddy
.Nd read and modify property list files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl cxlh
.Ar file.plist
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
edits the property list stored in
.Ar file.plist ,
creating it if it does not exist.
Without
.Fl c ,
it reads commands from standard input, one per line, after a
.Dq Command:
prompt.
Changes are kept in memory until a
.Cm Save
command, or, when commands come from
.Fl c ,
until all of them have run.
The file is always written back in XML form.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl c Ar command
Run
.Ar command
instead of reading commands interactively.
May be given more than once; the commands run in order.
.It Fl x
Print values as XML property lists where possible.
.It Fl l
Do not follow symbolic links anywhere in the path of
.Ar file.plist .
.It Fl h
Print the command reference and exit.
.El
.Sh COMMANDS
Command names are matched without regard to case.
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Cm Help
Print the command reference.
.It Cm Exit
Leave without saving.
.It Cm Save
Write the current property list to the file.
.It Cm Revert
Reload the file, discarding unsaved changes.
.It Cm Clear Op Ar type
Replace the whole property list with an empty root of
.Ar type ,
a dictionary by default.
.It Cm Print Op Ar entry
Print
.Ar entry ,
or the whole property list.
.It Cm Set Ar entry value
Change the value of an existing, non-container
.Ar entry .
.It Cm Add Ar entry type Op Ar value
Create
.Ar entry
with the given
.Ar type
and
.Ar value .
Everything after
.Ar type
is the value, spaces included.
.It Cm Copy Ar source destination
Copy the
.Ar source
entry to a new
.Ar destination
entry.
.It Cm Delete Ar entry
Remove
.Ar entry .
.It Cm Merge Oo Fl r Oc Ar file Op Ar entry
Add the contents of the property list in
.Ar file
to the container
.Ar entry ,
or to the current container.
Existing keys are skipped unless
.Fl r
is given, in which case containers of the same kind are merged recursively.
.It Cm Import Ar entry file
Set
.Ar entry
to the contents of
.Ar file ,
creating it as data if it does not exist.
.It Cm CD Ar entry
Make the container
.Ar entry
the current container for relative entries.
.El
.Sh ENTRIES
An entry is a list of keys separated by colons, starting from the root
when it begins with a colon and from the current container otherwise.
Array elements are named by their zero-based index; an empty index names
the end of the array.
A colon that is part of a key is written as
.Ql \e: .
.Pp
The types are
.Cm string ,
.Cm array ,
.Cm dict ,
.Cm bool ,
.Cm real ,
.Cm integer ,
.Cm date
and
.Cm data .
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Nm
exits 0 on success and 1 if any command failed.
.Sh EXAMPLES
Change a bundle identifier:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
PlistBuddy -c "Set :CFBundleIdentifier org.example.app" Info.plist
.Ed
.Pp
Append a dictionary to an array:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
PlistBuddy -c "Add :CFBundleDocumentTypes: dict" Info.plist
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr defaults 1 ,
.Xr plutil 1
